{
 "answer": "FDA does not require a cosmetics contract manufacturer to keep pest-control records such as trap maps, service reports, or pesticide logs under 21 CFR 700.27.\n\nThe available regulatory sources do not provide enough information to answer this.  \n\n[1] (Note: The provided evidence focuses exclusively on prohibited cattle materials, recordkeeping related to cattle material usage, and retention of records for compliance with the use of such materials. There is no mention of pest-control records, trap maps, service reports, or pesticide logs in any part of 21 CFR 700.27.)\nEvidence limit: not all of the retrieved text of 21 CFR 700.27 fit in the evidence supplied for this answer (6 paragraphs left out). The answer above does not cover that text; consult the full provisions.",
